<Doc title="Beta terms · Tracend" description="The terms for using the Tracend app during its private, invite-only beta.">
  <h1>Beta terms</h1>
  <p class="doc-date">Last updated 2 November 2026</p>
  <p class="doc-lede">These terms cover the Tracend app during its private beta. You accept them when you set up the app, and the app asks again whenever they change. Please read them with our <a href="/privacy/">privacy notice</a>.</p>

  <h2>A private beta</h2>
  <p>Tracend is unfinished and invite-only. Features may change, break or disappear, and we may pause or end the beta at any time. When we can, we tell you in the app or by email first.</p>

  <h2>Who can use it</h2>
  <p>Tracend is for healthy adults aged 18 or older. Don&rsquo;t use it if you are pregnant or have recently given birth, have or are recovering from an eating disorder, need a medically prescribed diet, have a serious or recent injury, need rehabilitation, or have a condition your doctor says needs supervised exercise. If the app&rsquo;s health check suggests you see a professional first, do that before you train with Tracend.</p>

  <h2>Not medical advice</h2>
  <p>Tracend gives general training and nutrition guidance. It is not a medical service: it does not diagnose, treat or monitor any condition, and it is not for emergencies. Talk to a doctor before you start a new training or eating plan, and whenever you are unsure whether something is safe for you. In an emergency, call your local emergency number.</p>

  <h2>Training is your choice</h2>
  <p>Exercise carries a risk of injury. You decide what you do, how much you lift and when you rest. Warm up, use loads you can control, and stop at once if you feel pain, chest pain, dizziness or unusual breathlessness; get medical help if it doesn&rsquo;t pass. Reporting pain in the app changes your training, but it is not an assessment of the pain.</p>

  <h2>AI and estimates can be wrong</h2>
  <p>Some features use AI models, and every plan, reply, meal estimate and suggestion they produce can be wrong or incomplete. Numbers worked out from your data, such as trends and targets, are estimates too. Nothing changes your plan, your meals or your records until you approve it. Use your own judgement, and ask a professional when it matters.</p>

  <h2>Your data</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/privacy/">privacy notice</a> explains what we collect and why. Using your health data needs its own agreement, which the app asks for separately from these terms, and each AI feature asks before it sends anything. You can export your data or delete your account at any time.</p>

  <h2>Your account and fair use</h2>
  <p>Your account is for you alone. Keep your password private and don&rsquo;t share your access. Don&rsquo;t misuse Tracend: no attempts to break, overload or get around its security or limits; no scraping, copying, reverse engineering or decompiling the app, except where the law gives you that right; no using it to harm anyone or to break the law; and no uploading photos of other people or content you have no right to share.</p>

  <h2>What belongs to whom</h2>
  <p>What you log and upload stays yours. You let us store and use it only to run Tracend for you, as the privacy notice describes. The app, its design and its content belong to Tracend; during the beta you may use them for your own training, and that permission ends when your access does.</p>

  <h2>Feedback</h2>
  <p>If you send us ideas, bug reports or other feedback, we may use them to improve Tracend without owing you anything for it. We never publish anything that identifies you without asking first.</p>

  <h2>Suspension and leaving</h2>
  <p>We may suspend or close an account that breaks these terms or puts others at risk, and we tell you why when we can. You can stop using Tracend at any time, and delete your account in the app under Account, then Delete account. Deleting it removes your data as the privacy notice describes.</p>

  <h2>No promises</h2>
  <p>To the extent the law allows, the beta is provided as it is and as available. We don&rsquo;t promise that it is accurate, complete, uninterrupted, free of errors or suited to any particular purpose.</p>

  <h2>Limits on our liability</h2>
  <p>To the extent the law allows, Tracend is not liable for indirect or consequential losses, such as lost data, profits or opportunities, or for injury that comes from training you chose to do. Nothing in these terms limits liability that the law does not allow us to limit, such as for fraud, or for death or personal injury caused by our negligence.</p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>If these terms change, we update this page and the date at the top, and the app asks you to agree again before you carry on. If you don&rsquo;t agree, you can sign out or delete your account from that same screen.</p>

  <h2>The law that applies</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of India, and the courts of India can hear any dispute about them. This doesn&rsquo;t take away any protection the law where you live gives you.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
</Doc>
